<title>CHINA: China customs seize smuggled magnesium ore.</title>
<headline>China customs seize smuggled magnesium ore.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Customs officials in China's Dalian city in northeastern Liaoning province have seized 3,600 tonnes of magnesium ore being smuggled out of the country, a local official said on Friday.</p>
<p>The magnesium ore, valued at 1.10 million yuan ($132,530), was uncovered by officials of the Bayuquan customs on a cargo ship heading for the United States, he said.</p>
<p>Magnesium ore can only be exported from China with an official permit, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;This is a serious case, they hold no export permit, they did not declare to customs,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>Police had detained a suspect and were investigating the case, he said, but gave no further details.</p>
<p>($=8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
